// Jest Snapshot v1, https://jestjs.io/docs/snapshot-testing

exports[`CLI help interface for 'idm remote-proxy test' should be expected english 1`] = `
"Usage: frodo idm remote-proxy test [options] [host] [realm] [username] [password]

[Cloud-only] Test an IDM remote proxy.

Makes one read through the proxy to the receiving tenant. A working proxy
answers with the identity and roles it is mapped to there, which shows that the
token request, the static user mapping and the routing all work. A proxy that
does not work is explained: the ESV changes it needs were not applied yet, the
token request failed, or the static user mapping is missing. Nothing is changed.

Arguments:
  host                       AM base URL, e.g.: https://cdk.iam.example.com/am.
                             To use a connection profile, just specify a unique
                             substring or alias.
  realm                      Realm. Specify realm as '/' for the root realm or
                             'realm' or '/parent/child' otherwise. (default:
                             "alpha" for Identity Cloud tenants, "/" otherwise.)
  username                   Username to login with. Must be an admin user with
                             appropriate rights to manage authentication
                             journeys/trees. If given without a password, and it
                             matches the username already stored in the
                             connection profile for the target host, frodo uses
                             that profile's stored password instead of requiring
                             it on the command line.
  password                   Password.

Deployment: Cloud-only

Options:
  -i, --proxy-id <proxy-id>  Remote proxy name. (pick from remote proxy)
                             (prompts if missing)
  --json                     Output in JSON format.
  -h, --help                 Help
  -hh, --help-more           Help with all options.
  -hhh, --help-all           Help with all options, environment variables, and
                             usage examples.
"
`;
